Wolfi deviation 2 of 2 (docs/deviations.md, "PXC entrypoint pwmake"): as in percona-server-docker-scripts,
MYSQL_RANDOM_ROOT_PASSWORD uses pwmake (libpwquality); Wolfi has no pwmake. 24 random bytes from /dev/urandom as
48 hex characters (192 bits of entropy) with od and tr (busybox). Same output contract: one printable, shell-safe
string.

--- a/percona-xtradb-cluster-9.x/dockerdir/entrypoint.sh	2026-11-17 09:33:16.346888937 +0200
+++ b/percona-xtradb-cluster-9.x/dockerdir/entrypoint.sh	2026-11-17 09:33:16.351888932 +0200
@@ -238,7 +238,7 @@
 		fi
 
 		if [ ! -z "$MYSQL_RANDOM_ROOT_PASSWORD" ]; then
-			MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD="$(pwmake 128)"
+			MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD="$(od -An -N24 -tx1 /dev/urandom | tr -d " \n")"
 			echo "GENERATED ROOT PASSWORD: $MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD"
 		fi
 
